+/*
+ * Composition of layered child windows over their top-level.
+ *
+ * On Windows 8 and later the DWM blends a child painted through
+ * UpdateLayeredWindow() over everything its top-level shows, including the
+ * children of other processes, live.  Here such a child has no X window (see
+ * is_ulw_child()), so while one is visible the top-level is redirected: every
+ * painter, the owner's surface flush, its GL presents and the GDI of other
+ * processes alike, draws into a backing pixmap published on the top-level, and
+ * only the owner writes the X window, composing that pixmap with an overlay
+ * holding the layered children.  XDamage on the backing pixmap is the only
+ * notice the owner gets of another process drawing; a thread of its own waits
+ * for it on a connection of its own, since the application's threads read
+ * their X events only when they pump messages, and a plug-in host's GUI thread
+ * may do that seldom.  iZotope Trash shows its preset list this way over a
+ * WebView2 window of another process; blending over the X window instead let
+ * every WebView2 frame wipe the list and every GL present wipe the frame.
+ */
+
